  "analysis": "\n\n• **1. Atelier Bois & Co (d5, d6) | €6 250 | 2 docs**\n  - *Ambiguity*: d5 targets \"4 rue du Port\" (LMNP) but addressee \"Mme Morel\"; d6 targets sterilization room but addressee \"Dr Morel\" with no site. Settle by confirming site vs entity.\n  - *Question*: \"Do these carpenter documents relate to the LMNP flat or the SELARL clinic?\"\n  - *Rules*: d5=LMNP, d6=SELARL → always LMNP/SELARL (depends on discriminator: site address); Both SELARL → always SELARL; Both LMNP → always LMNP.\n• **2. Prévia Assurances (d1, d2, d3) | €1 704 | 3 docs**\n  - *Ambiguity*: d1 is Hélène’s PER debited from SELARL (\"Prélèvement sur le compte FR76...\"); d2 is Paul’s personal policy; d3 is Hélène’s cover paid by SELARL. Settle by confirming contract owner vs payer.\n  - *Question*: \"Are these Prévia contracts personal or business-linked?\"\n  - *Rules*: All personal → always personal; d1/d3 business, d2 personal → always SELARL/Personal (depends on discriminator: insured person); d1 reimbursed → always SELARL/Personal.\n• **3. Paul/LMNP Allocation (d4, d7) | €689,99 | 2 docs**\n  - *Ambiguity*: d4 is a joint statement receiving LMNP rent (\"LOYER 4 RUE DU PORT MAI 650,00\"); d7 is Paul’s telecom bill at the LMNP address. Settle by confirming account/bill ownership vs business use.\n  - *Question*: \"Should the joint account (d4) and Paul’s telecom bill (d7) be personal or allocated to LMNP?\"\n  - *Rules*: Both personal → always personal; Both LMNP → always LMNP; Mixed → ask each time.",
